  "items": [
    {
      "_id": "hHkhwZRVshhubbfG",
      "name": "Checkpoint Reality",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/time/hourglass-tilted-gray.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>When the Oracle would be reduced to 0 hit points or killed outright, they may instead establish a saved state of existence that the causing event cannot retroactively violate: the damage is undone and the Oracle returns to the position they held at the start of the turn. Green T put a bullet through the Oracle's brain. The Oracle did not heal it, dodge it, or shield against it. The Oracle checkpointed, and the bullet stopped having happened.</p><p><em>Once per day. This is a temporal function, not a defensive spell.</em></p>",
          "chat": "The event stops having happened."
        },
        "type": {
          "value": "monster",
          "subtype": ""
